course: dictionary
lesson: 11196
title: Withdraw and its many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Withdraw is a verb, which means it is a doing word. Its forms are withdraw, withdraws, withdrew, withdrawn and withdrawing. The words around it give you the clues. «She went to the bank to withdraw ten pounds.» The bank and the pounds tell you withdraw means take money out.
explain: «He withdrew from the race because of his sore ankle.» Ask yourself: what would fit here? Stop taking part, or take out? Try your meaning in the sentence. Stopping the race fits, and the sore ankle explains why he stopped.
explain: Withdraw can also mean move back or go quiet. «The shy girl withdrew to a corner and hardly spoke all day.» Her quietness is the clue: she moved away from people and kept to herself. The same word can have several meanings, so always check the clues.
fact: Withdraw means to take something out, to move back, to stop taking part, to take back what you said, or to go quiet.
fact: «Withdraw money» means take money out of a bank account.
fact: «Withdraw from» means stop taking part in something, such as a race or a match.
fact: «Withdraw a remark» means take back something you said.
fact: «Withdrew» is the past tense of withdraw: «Simone Biles withdrew from events in Tokyo to protect herself.»
exercise: «She went to the bank to withdraw ten pounds.» What does withdraw mean here? | *Take money out of an account | Lend money to a friend | Count the coins in a jar | Put money into an account
exercise: «After one lap, the runner withdrew from the race because of a sore foot.» What does withdrew mean? | Won the race | *Stopped taking part | Started the race early | Ran faster than everyone
exercise: Withdraw is a verb. Which word is the past tense of withdraw? | withdraw | withdraws | *withdrew | withdrawing
test: «After the argument, Sam said he would withdraw what he had said.» What does withdraw mean here? | Say it louder | Shout it again | *Take back | Write it down
test: «Armies may withdraw from the city when peace is agreed.» What does withdraw mean here? | *Move back or away | Build a new wall | Open a new road | Win the battle
exam: «Bottling up strong feelings can make children withdrawn.» What does withdrawn most likely mean? | Rich and famous | Happy to share everything | *Quiet and keeping away from others | Full of energy and loud
